Claim 08 — Build gate (capture exit codes, block on failure)
============================================================

Goal: confirm that the goal system captures real build/test command
output and exit codes, and blocks task completion when the configured
gate fails — rather than trusting an LLM self-assessment such as "tests
pass".

Method: static inspection only (Grep + Read) of
src/goal/build-gate.ts and src/goal/agent-executor.ts.

1. Real subprocess capture (not LLM self-report)
------------------------------------------------

   src/goal/build-gate.ts:65-115

       export function runBuildGateCommands(commands: string[], workingDir: string): BuildGateResult {
         for (const command of commands) {
           ...
           const result = spawnSync("bash", ["-lc", trimmed], {
             cwd: workingDir,
             encoding: "utf8",
             timeout: BUILD_GATE_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS,
             maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024,
           });
           const stdout = typeof result.stdout === "string" ? result.stdout : "";
           const stderr = typeof result.stderr === "string" ? result.stderr : "";
           const output = truncateForPrompt([stdout, stderr].filter(Boolean).join("\n"));

           if (result.error) {
             ...
             return { passed: false, failedCommand: trimmed, output: ..., failureKind: ... };
           }

           if (result.status !== 0) {
             ...
             return { passed: false, failedCommand: trimmed, output: ..., failureKind: ... };
           }
         }
         return { passed: true };
       }

   Each configured gate command is spawned through bash and produces a
   real `result.status` (exit code) plus captured stdout/stderr. The
   function returns `{ passed: false, ..., failedCommand, output }`
   whenever the spawn errors out or exits non-zero — the worker's own
   "I'm done" report has no influence on this branch.

   Build-gate output is truncated for prompt re-use, not for the gate
   decision (build-gate.ts:24-29).

2. Per-step gate runs AFTER the worker claims complete
------------------------------------------------------

   src/goal/agent-executor.ts:532-577

       const gateCommands = plan.buildGate?.commands?.map((cmd) => cmd.trim()).filter(Boolean) ?? [];
       if (
         task.status === "done" &&
         plan.buildGate?.runBetweenSteps === true &&
         gateCommands.length > 0
       ) {
         ...
         const gateResult = runBuildGateCommands(commandsForThisStep, workingDir);
         const timestamp = new Date().toISOString();
         if (gateResult.passed) {
           session.buildGateResults[task.id] = { passed: true, timestamp };
           ...
         } else {
           session.buildGateResults[task.id] = {
             passed: false,
             failedCommand: gateResult.failedCommand,
             output: gateResult.output,
             timestamp,
           };

   Critical ordering:

     a. The CLI worker reports `status = "done"`.
     b. Only THEN does the agent loop call runBuildGateCommands().
     c. The persisted record `session.buildGateResults[task.id]` is the
        gate result, not the worker's self-report.

3. Failure path — blocks or reverts; never silently confirms
------------------------------------------------------------

   src/goal/agent-executor.ts:579-661

       if (gateResult.failureKind === "infra_failed") {
         ...
         task.status = "blocked";
         task.blockedReason = "task_failed";
         task.blockedQuestion = `Build gate infrastructure failed.\n${detail}`;
         task.failedDetail = {
           whatTried: detail,
           errorType: "build_gate_infra_failed",
           ...
         };
       } else {
         const fixCount = (buildGateFixCounts.get(task.id) ?? 0) + 1;
         ...
         if (fixCount > DEFAULT_MAX_BUILD_GATE_FIX_CYCLES) {
           ...
           task.status = "blocked";
           task.blockedReason = "task_failed";
           task.blockedQuestion = `Build gate failed after ${DEFAULT_MAX_BUILD_GATE_FIX_CYCLES} retry cycles.\n${detail}`;
           task.failedDetail = {
             whatTried: detail,
             errorType: "build_gate_failed",
             ...
           };
         } else {
           const reset = resetToTaskBaseSha(
             workingDir,
             session.taskCheckpoints?.[task.id]?.baseSha,
           );
           if (!reset.success) {
             task.status = "blocked";
             ...
             errorType: "build_gate_reset_failed",
             ...
           } else {
             ...
             writeAttemptBundle(workerDir, syntheticBundle);
             appendRetryContext(runId, task.id, ..., syntheticBundle.attemptNumber);
             appendGoalWorkingEntry(
               runId,
               task.id,
               "build-gate",
               `Build gate failed (${fixCount}/${DEFAULT_MAX_BUILD_GATE_FIX_CYCLES}) on ${gateResult.failedCommand}. Retrying after reset.`,
             );
             task.status = "pending";
             ...
           }
         }
       }

   Three concrete consequences when the gate fails (none of which let
   the worker's "done" report stand):

     * `task.status = "blocked"` on infra failure
       (agent-executor.ts:581-590).
     * `task.status = "blocked"` on retry exhaustion
       (agent-executor.ts:598-607).
     * Otherwise: reset working tree to the task checkpoint base SHA
       (agent-executor.ts:609-612 via resetToTaskBaseSha — see
       build-gate.ts:195-211) and reset `task.status = "pending"` for a
       retry (agent-executor.ts:654-657). A synthetic AttemptBundle
       with `outcome: "failed"` and
       `errorClassification: "build_gate_failure"` is written so the
       next attempt sees the real failure context
       (agent-executor.ts:629-641).

4. Final gate after all tasks claim done
----------------------------------------

   src/goal/agent-executor.ts:739-757

       if (allDone && finalGateCommands.length > 0) {
         const finalGateResult = runBuildGateCommands(finalGateCommands, workingDir);
         const timestamp = new Date().toISOString();
         if (finalGateResult.passed) {
           session.buildGateResults["__final__"] = { passed: true, timestamp };
         } else {
           session.buildGateResults["__final__"] = {
             passed: false,
             failedCommand: finalGateResult.failedCommand,
             output: finalGateResult.output,
             timestamp,
           };
           ...
           finalBuildGateFailurePrompt = `Final build gate failed.\n${detail}`;
           session.lastError = `Final build gate failed on ${finalGateResult.failedCommand}.`;
         }
       }

       if (allDone && !finalBuildGateFailurePrompt) {
         session.state = "done";

   The session only transitions to `state = "done"` when the final gate
   actually passed (agent-executor.ts:760-761). When the final gate
   fails the session stays non-done and the failure prompt is fed back
   into the loop.

Summary of the "block on failure, do not trust LLM" claim
---------------------------------------------------------

  * The system spawns the gate commands itself in a real subprocess
    (build-gate.ts:70).
  * It evaluates the actual exit code (build-gate.ts:94).
  * On failure it overrides `task.status = "done"` to either `"blocked"`
    or `"pending"` (agent-executor.ts:581, 598, 654).
  * `session.state = "done"` is gated on the final gate passing
    (agent-executor.ts:760).

Safe README wording
-------------------

  * "Code-related steps only count as complete when the configured
    build/test commands actually exit zero. Failed gate output is fed
    back to the worker for retry, or the step is blocked."
  * "The session reaches a `done` state only after the final build gate
    passes."

Unsafe wording to avoid
-----------------------

  * "Trust the agent — it self-verifies it ran tests." The gate runs
    independently of the worker's self-report.
  * "Build always passes before merge." Moltbot does not own merge; the
    gate guards the in-loop state transition, not the upstream git
    workflow.

STATUS: verified
REASON: runBuildGateCommands captures real exit code + stdout/stderr
via spawnSync (build-gate.ts:65-115); the agent-executor loop calls it
after the worker reports `status = "done"` and overrides that status
to `blocked` or `pending` on failure (agent-executor.ts:565-661);
session-level `done` is conditional on the final gate passing
(agent-executor.ts:739-761).
